# Line endings, decided here rather than by whoever cloned this.
#
# Everything in this directory is read by Linux: bash runs the scripts, systemd
# reads the unit, Docker reads the compose file. Checked out with CRLF — which
# is what git does by default on Windows, where this repository is developed —
# bash reads the shebang as `/usr/bin/env bash\r`, cannot find it, and reports
#
#     /usr/bin/env: 'bash\r': No such file or directory
#
# naming an interpreter that is plainly installed. `eol=lf` applies on checkout
# too, so a Windows working tree gets LF for these whatever `core.autocrlf` is
# set to locally. Portal-Docker/.gitattributes does the same for its own files.

* text=auto

*.sh       text eol=lf
*.yml      text eol=lf
*.service  text eol=lf
*.example  text eol=lf
